  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - Due to the scale of the proposed building together with the inclusion of primary living facilities the proposal would fail to relate incidentally or subordinately to the main dwelling appearing as an overly dominant addition resulting in harm to the character and appearance of the local area contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, SC7 and SC1 as well as the council's design guidance.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would result in harm to the amenity of neighbouring occupiers through increased levels of activity and different patterns of use at the foot of the amenity area which would affect the quiet enjoyment of the rear garden space enjoyed by neighbouring occupiers, furthermore, due to its scale and relationship with neighbouring dwelling at 71 Harvest Road represent a visually intrusive form of development contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2 and SC7 as well as the council's design guidance."
